g real life problems  using cutting-edge technologies  this clearly displays the qualification  of the candidate along with her career  interest  you could tailor the headline to meet  your interest and you could also add a  few keywords from the jd  the next tip to keep in mind before  proceeding to the body of your resume is  to make sure to add your contact  information  this might be an obvious step however  missing this will be a huge loss  your contact information will be used by  recruiters to contact you  here you can incorporate information  like your name phone number and email id  you can also add your address resumes  can also have your professional profiles  for better credibility  you could add your linkedin profile link  and github link  now with many interviews happening  online you can also mention your skype  id  make sure that every detail you give is  right and it must look professional  shown alongside we have given details  like email id  phone number place of residence linkedin  profile link and github profile links  since the name is already on the resume  it needn't be added again  make sure to always add your full name  on your resume and it is also great if  you could have a professional image of  yourself on the top most corner of your  resume  moving to contact details having your  address generally helps if you're  looking for a job within a particular  distance from your home  you could also elaborate on the address  the next tip to keep in mind is to have  a professional looking email address on  your resume  it is always advice that you have your  personal phone number on the resume to  keep the job search confidential  as shown alongside always place your  contact information on top  so that it can be easily noticed by the  recruiters  and make sure that you align them well  moving on to filling in the body of your  resume our next tip is to highlight your  educational details  like mentioned previously this resume  that we are building is for freshers  hence the first part of our resume can  be the educational qualifications  education is one of the main areas  employers look for on your resume  it is another way for an employer to  comprehend if you are the right fit  for the role if your education aligns  with the posted job role it can be a  huge advantage  so how to go about feeding your  education and details and what are the  details you need to have  let's look at that now this section of  educational qualification should have  the name of your most recent degree  name of your university and location if  possible  following which you must mention the  dates attended and your graduation date  or expected graduation date if you're  still studying  the next part should be your scores in  cgpa or percentage  better the scores the better your resume  looks  you could also add any academic honors  or relevant coursework or study abroad  programs  if you have two degrees always start  with your highest degree first  as shown alongside you can have the name  of the degree  below which you can have the university  name start  and end date of the course and finally  the cgpa  similarly we have another section of the  school details below the college details  it is good to show your school details  as well you can follow the same drill  for this too  if you wish you can have another section  below this for additional educational  details  and mention the certifications you  possess and any presented papers  we have shown that in a separate section  of this resume we shall look at it in  our further slides  the next section is one of the most  important areas of a resume  this is your skill section remember to  highlight your skills in a way that  recruiters find them relevant to the job  role you are applying for  you could choose a set of hard skills  and soft skills that you possess  and additionally you could sprinkle a  few skills that are mentioned in the job  description  skills can be your natural talents or  the job expertise you have developed  over time  your skills should make the employers  feel that you have the required  abilities to succeed in the respective  job role  skills can often be the deciding factor  when it comes to proceeding with your  candidature  you can mention hard skills they are  basically technical skills that revolve  around your job profile  on the other hand soft skills may be  referred to as social or people skills  these skills like communication  adaptability problem solving and  leadership to name a few are soft skills  as shown alongside in this sample resume  for freshers  we have mentioned a few technical skills  while listing your skills it is wise to  use a two-column format that names the  skills and your level of experience with  the skill  here we have taken skills that are  primarily relevant in the data analytics  sector  you could change these skills depending  on the profile you are applying for  as you can see not only are you just  mentioning the skill but you are also  evaluating your expertise in it  if all the file boxes are colored it  shows you're proficient in it and vice  versa  this is a good way to showcase your  skills and it becomes  easier for the recruiters to identify  how good you are in the listed skills  our advice to you is to have the  relevant skills for the job you are  applying for  stay updated with the growing technology  and make sure your most recent skills  are reflected on your resume  here we have chosen skills like python  r machine learning data visualization  tableau and sql  the next section is another important  section on the freshers resume  as you are a fresher you might be  wondering how to convince the recruiters  of your skills and expertise  the best way to do so is by adding your  project details and internship  experience if any  since you have no work experience these  details can prove that you are fit to  start your career  in the previous section we saw how  important it is to list your skills  and in this section you should be able  to highlight hands-on cases of how you  have applied your skills  and capabilities to find a solution  you can first mention the name of the  project following which you could  mention the duration for the same  and then list out a few vital points as  to what you did  make sure to keep the content short and  crisp  depending on how you have carried out  the project your leadership qualities  can also be gauged by the hiring manager  remember to list relevant projects to  the job role you are applying for  as seen alongside under the project  section we have three projects  they are twitter sentiment analysis face  recognition  and uber data analysis you can notice  the duration given below each of these  projects  following which we have just a few  sentences on what our role was in the  project  these project details mentioned on this  sample resume can be of great value when  it comes to the field of data analytics  similarly it is advised that you add  relevant project details pertaining to  your field of interest  in addition to this you could also  consider adding a link to your online  portfolio if it has additional details  of your project  by doing so they will be able to see the  projects you have worked on  and how suitable your candidature is  here you can also add few details of  your internship if you have any  remember having internship details on  your resume is definitely a plus point  and it counts as a good experience  the next section on our resume is  extracurricular activities  it is imperative that you include  extracurricular activities on your  resume especially for freshers  as you lack work experience this is  where you realize how important  it is to be active in school and college  activities  so if you are one of those active  students then go ahead and showcase your  skills to prove your capabilities  under this section you can add any  activity that comes outside the scope of  your college or school curriculum  in this sample resume we have divided  the sections of extracurricular  activities  for better clarity and since this is a  freshers resume we have done so  the first thing you can have under this  section is any kind of participation in  webinars  workshops clubs etc as you see on the  screen  first here we have participation in  webinars and workshops related to data  science and machine learning  then we are listing the role of the  candidate as a part of the sponsorship  committee for tech events and cultural  fests  finally we are talking about a  non-technical activity that is the  formation of a plantation club to create  awareness  among people on environmental issues so  as you see we have three different kinds  of activities here  similarly you could go on and add any  kind of activity like part of the  student government  any college clubs volunteer work and  study abroad experience to name a few  now the next section we have is for  achievements  this section can be used by not just  experienced professionals but also by  freshers  here you could add any competitions you  have won in your student life  or any other sort of recognition you  have been awarded with  you can also add any scholarships if you  have received  it is great to mention these details on  your resume as it will make your  candidature look  good on the whole make sure to list only  those details that are true  as you can see here we have mentioned  securing fifth rank in a hackathon on  python programming  and then achieving a certificate of  recognition  for successfully organizing a startup  summit in college  so both these are achievements of the  candidate and for which she has been  duly recognized  there is absolutely no harm in  displaying your awards and recognitions  on your resume  next section on our resume is for your  certifications  so if you're looking to add your  certifications on your resume  this section can be well utilized  however if your certification is  job critical you could add them on top  of your resume as a part of your  headline as well  in other cases you can add it under this  section  so why is it important to have a  certification well because it proves  that you have specific expertise and  because it is issued by an authorized  organization  many jobs require you to hold certain  certifications  and sometimes more than one certificate  and if you are working in sectors like  accounting or finance  they definitely require licenses and  certifications  so the types of certificates vary across  sectors  a professional certification provides  evidence of your skills  and is proof that you have the required  work competence  certifications can certainly boost your  resume and help you stand apart from the  rest  your first duty is to put the relevant  certifications which align with the job  description  this will help the recruiter notice your  resume quickly  certifications are often used as a  resume filter by employers to narrow the  pool of applicants  for example an it security professional  could have relevant networking  certificates  to make his profile look more appealing  particularly if you are an entry-level  candidate or a student  listing relevant and in-demand  certificates will make your resume stand  out  at times recommended certificates can be  found in the job description as well  as shown alongside here we have the  candidate listing the completion of the  postgraduate program in data analytics  offered by simplylearn  the candidate is also a certified data  analyst professional from ibm  she holds a certification from google  for completing crash course on python  and she finally is also certified in  business analytics with excel course  that is offered by simply learn  reading these points will definitely  leave a lasting impression on the hiring  manager  and it will make you look more driven  and committed to your field of study  you need to regularly stay updated with  the ever evolving technology in order to  bag your dream job  on that note you all can check out the  simplylearn website to upscale yourself  and choose any certification from the  many options we have  having a certification will help you  develop skills for your career growth  simplylearn provides a cutting-edge  curriculum designed and guidance with  industry to develop job-ready skills  and the best part about these  certifications being that you can learn  by working on real world problems  here you will have projects involving  real-world data sets with virtual labs  for hands-on learning  so what are you waiting for get  certified with simply learn and upskill  yourself  next section on our list is about  languages  this section can be very impressive if  it is utilized well  so you might speak a second language but  you're unsure if it needs to be added on  your resume  well it definitely should go on your  resume the more languages the better  your candidature will look  knowing a second language also displays  cultural knowledge  you can flaunt your language skills to  your advantage here being proficient in  multiple languages can open a range of  opportunities in your professional life  listing your language skills can surely  make your resume more noticeable  communication is a critical part of any  job and recruiters often look for  language skills as they show  your capability to communicate with a  diverse range of people  the language skills on your resume could  include any other languages in which you  have intermediate advanced proficient on  native comprehension abilities  if a particular language can be  beneficial for the job role you're  applying for  then you need to have that language on  your resume as it may be a nice benefit  for the employer as well  if you know a foreign language it is  great as you can use your expertise to  communicate  well with international partners without  going through  an interpreter or a translator as you  can see alongside here we have two  languages  english and french it says english full  professional proficiency  and french limited working proficiency  it is good to have your level of  proficiency mentioned beside the  language as it will help the recruiter  understand how good you are in that  particular language  so before mentioning languages on your  resume you must review your speaking  reading and listening comprehension of  the language  and then add your proficiency level if  you know other regional languages  feel free to add those as well under  this section  language skills can surely help you grow  your professional network and provide  you ample job opportunities and help you  display your soft skills  the next section we have is for your  hobbies and interests  some of you might be unsure whether you  should include these on your resumes  well you definitely can it is best if  you add hobbies and interests that have  some form of relevance to the job you  are interested in  and let the hiring manager know you are  a good fit for the job  you could also do so by tailoring your  interests and by providing a variety of  hobbies  for example if you notice that the job  you're applying for wants outgoing  candidates  who are good team players then you need  to tailor your list of hobbies around  this  this way you can make use of this  section to your advantage  be sure to include your hobbies and  interests towards the end of your resume  keep this section short and do frame  your interests creatively  as seen we have a few interests here  like reading  traveling cooking and gardening on our  resume you could also add your hobbies  and interests accordingly  the next tip to you is to be honest  while crafting your resume  ensure you don't add any false  information as it will leave a  bad mark on your profile forever you  think honesty might not be the best  policy in this case  but it very well is still the best  policy even when it comes to building  your resume  recruiters can easily understand if  you're exaggerating and if your resume  looks to be  more of a fiction than fact for example  you cannot lie that you have passed out  from an ivy league university when the  reality is totally different  keep in mind that your educational  background will be checked by the  recruiters  similarly you cannot say you're  proficient in everything as  employers very well realize how much  people exaggerate their skill set  in such cases you'll be caught when  asked to demonstrate your skill set  also keep in mind that your job title  shouldn't look too good to be true  another most common mistake is trying to  cover a career gap in the wrong way  and you will be caught if the recruiter  does a thorough background check  if you are worried about a resume gap  fill it with any sort of consulting or  volunteering work  and not with false information  finally our last tip to you is to  proofread your resume  nothing can be worse than having typos  or grammatical errors on your resume  check for spelling mistakes and sentence  structure having such errors will leave  a bad impression on the recruiter  and you might seem careless in addition  to this  make sure your resume is well formatted  and you use the same font type  throughout your resume  sometimes employers can be quite picky  when it comes to hiring  hence the smallest typo on your cover  letter or resume might prevent you from  getting the job  proofreading ensures that your document  is free of errors and polished well  without proofreading our work has a  higher chance of containing errors  ask your family member or a friend to  proofread your resume as a favor  as having another person evaluating your  resume will be more beneficial  after incorporating all the about 10  tips that we have discussed  remember to share only the pdf version  of your resume with the recruiters  now let's have a look at the final  version of our s